  "helpContactsSummary": "Your address book: people and organizations you keep in touch with.",
  "helpContactsAddTitle": "Add contact",
  "helpContactsAddBody": "Creates a new contact, either a person or an organization.",
  "helpContactsSearchTitle": "Search",
  "helpContactsSearchBody": "Type to filter contacts by name, phone or email. Chinese names also match their pinyin, written out (zhangwei) or as initials (zw).",
  "helpContactsSelfTitle": "Me",
  "helpContactsSelfBody": "The Me contact holds your own details and is marked with a Me badge. Switching on \"This is me\" in the edit form marks it and files it under the Me relationship. Tap it to view or edit them.",
  "helpContactDetailTitle": "Contact",
  "helpContactDetailSummary": "Everything saved about this contact.",
  "helpContactDetailCallTitle": "Call",
  "helpContactDetailCallBody": "Tap a phone number to call it.",
  "helpContactDetailMapTitle": "Open in maps",
  "helpContactDetailMapBody": "Tap an address to see it on a map. Addresses written in Chinese open in Google Maps (the app if installed), which finds Chinese addresses that Apple Maps can't.",
  "helpContactDetailEditTitle": "Edit",
  "helpContactDetailEditBody": "Change this contact's name, details or relationship.",
  "helpContactDetailRemoveTitle": "Remove",
  "helpContactDetailRemoveBody": "Removes this contact from your list. Tap Undo right after to bring it back.",
  "contactEnglishName": "English name",
  "contactEnglishNameHint": "Optional. For cheatsheets shown to English speakers.",
  "helpContactEditEnglishNameTitle": "English name",
  "helpContactEditEnglishNameBody": "Shown for a name written in Chinese. Add the English name this person or organization uses, such as Michael Wang. It doesn't change how the contact is shown or sorted in your list, but search finds it, and a cheatsheet row can show it (pick Contact.englishName) for a card meant for English speakers.",
  "helpContactEditTitle": "Edit contact",
  "helpContactEditSummary": "Enter the contact's name and details, then save.",
  "helpContactEditTypeTitle": "Person or organization",
  "helpContactEditTypeBody": "Choose whether this is a person or an organization. This decides which name fields you see.",
  "helpContactEditFieldsTitle": "Phones, emails and addresses",
  "helpContactEditFieldsBody": "Add as many as you need and label each one, such as Mobile or Work. For phones, tap the code beside the number to pick a country calling code, or paste a number that starts with +.",
  "helpContactEditAddressTitle": "Addresses",
  "helpContactEditAddressBody": "Pick the country for each address. United States, Canada and China get their own fields in that country's order: street, unit, city, state or province (pick from the list) and ZIP or postal code; for China, province, city, district, detailed address and postal code. A postal code in the wrong format is flagged and the contact will not save until it is fixed. Switching country keeps the street, city and postal code but clears the state or province and the district. Choose Other to type any address as free text over several lines. Switching to Other keeps what you entered as text.",
  "helpContactEditRelationshipTitle": "Relationship",
  "helpContactEditRelationshipBody": "How this contact relates to you. For example, a family doctor is a Doctor. Choose Other to describe it yourself.",
  "helpContactEditSelfTitle": "This is me",
  "helpContactEditSelfBody": "Marks this contact as yourself. Only one contact can be marked.",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletTitle": "Cheatsheets",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletSummary": "Your cards at a glance. Tap a card to open it; use search and the chips to narrow the wallet.",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletTilesTitle": "Cards",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletTilesBody": "Each card shows its colour or cover photo, its icon, its title, and its group with the number of rows. Tap a card to open it.",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletGroupsTitle": "Group chips",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletGroupsBody": "The first row of chips shows one wallet group at a time; All shows every card again. Search works within the chosen group.",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletTagsTitle": "Tag chips",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletTagsBody": "Tag chips narrow the wallet to cards that carry every tag you select. Tap a tag again to drop it.",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletLockTitle": "Lock badge",
  "helpCheatsheetWalletLockBody": "A lock marks a protected card. A 🔒 means its cover photo is locked in the vault: the card shows its colour instead, and opening the card lets you unlock the photo.",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailTitle": "Cheatsheet",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailSummary": "One card, its rows filled from your notes. Edit or delete it from the top bar.",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailFactsTitle": "Facts layout",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailFactsBody": "Each row shows its label with the value from your note underneath. A dash means the row is not linked yet; \"source removed\" means its note was deleted. Tap a phone number or an address to call or map it.",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailKeyPointsTitle": "Key points layout",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailKeyPointsBody": "Rows are numbered on the card's colour, each with its emoji if one was chosen, the label in bold and the value below. Values, actions and photos work as in Facts.",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailOpenSourceTitle": "Open the note",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailOpenSourceBody": "Tap the open button on a row to see where its value comes from. A contact opens on its contact screen; other notes open as notes. Long-press the row to see the raw note instead.",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailHeaderTitle": "Cover header",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailHeaderBody": "The top of the card shows its colour and pattern or its cover photo, its icon, its title, and its group with the number of rows. Change the look in the designer.",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailLockTitle": "Locked cover",
  "helpCheatsheetDetailLockBody": "When the cover photo is protected and the vault is locked, the header shows a lock tile instead. Tap it to unlock and see the photo.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerTitle": "Designing a cheatsheet",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerSummary": "Name the card, choose how it looks, then point each row at a piece of a note.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerLookTitle": "Look",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerLookBody": "Look holds the colour, pattern, icon, cover and layout. It starts open on a new card and folded on an existing one; tap its header to open or fold it. The small tile in the header previews the card as it will appear in the wallet.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerIconTitle": "Icon",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerIconBody": "Choose an emoji for the card. Search in English or Chinese, or type any emoji yourself.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerCoverTitle": "Cover photo",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerCoverBody": "Take a photo, choose one from your photos or scan a document to use as the card's background; a dark band behind the title keeps the text readable. Remove it any time and the colour comes back. Covers are available in Local and Cloud Storage modes.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerLayoutTitle": "Layout",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerLayoutBody": "Facts shows each label beside its value. Key points numbers the rows and colours them with the card's theme, which suits books and documents.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerSourceTitle": "Choose a note for a row",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerSourceBody": "Tap the link line under a row to choose where its value comes from. The Notes screen opens with its search, tags and filters; tap the note, then choose a field, a section, a photo or the whole note. Back from that step returns to the Notes screen.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerRowEmojiTitle": "Row emoji",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerRowEmojiBody": "In Key points, each row can carry its own emoji. Switching to Facts hides them without deleting them.",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerResetTitle": "Reset look",
  "helpCheatsheetDesignerResetBody": "Returns the colour, pattern, icon and layout to the template's defaults, removes the cover photo (in Cloud API mode the cover is kept) and clears every row emoji.",
